  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: f58b49e4622794818a5c8709faebf06a, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::BookContent
  text: "Keyword Cipher\n\nA Keyword Cipher is a modification of a Caesar cipher
    that utilizes a \u201Ckeyword\u201D to shift the letters of an encoded message.
    By matching the alphabet to the keyword (omitting any duplicate letters) and
    then filling in the rest of the alphabet, you can convert all letters from the
    top row to their corresponding letter on the bottom row. \n\nExample:\n \nABCDEFGHIJKLMNOPQRSTUVWXYZ\nKEYWORDABCFGHIJLMNPQSTUVXZ\n\nKeyword:
    Keyword\nPlain Text: Encoded Message\nEncoded Text: oiyjwow hoppkdo\n\nHere A
    becomes K, B becomes E, and so on. When we encode a message we just go letter
    by letter with the new alphabet, decoding is the inverse. "
